<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic8b42dcb1f391639a7048a5d20270ae9dac29dd3" commit="ac8e5379ad22a03e78169c4af3ad2977591fc98b" commit_message="platform_FilePerms/security_AccountsBaseline: Update debugfs-access uid/gid to 605  CQ-DEPEND=CL:364423 BUG=b:29873151 TEST=platform_FilePerms, security_AccountsBaseline  Change-Id: Ic8b42dcb1f391639a7048a5d20270ae9dac29dd3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/375582 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="375582" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/82/375582/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib6439c4be1c89fe043aeea00c8d0e350990e218c" commit="74acdb2b67d988b86cf001d0389228dee9be101f" commit_message="Change debugfs-access UID/GID to 605  We are going to share this group between Chrome OS and Android. It is only used to give permissions in specific files in debugfs _tracing_ directory.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:375582 BUG=b:29873151 TEST=build_image, check that debugfs-access gid is 605  Change-Id: Ib6439c4be1c89fe043aeea00c8d0e350990e218c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/364423 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="364423" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/eclass-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/eclass-overlay" ref="refs/changes/23/364423/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I43d9dd63f2c1cc58f2e98f19b290eb044e7c8890" commit="755a9240550783593dbb588615c5536af5a2abca" commit_message="Reorder list of options to test  Corresponds to r1485 from upstream. Commit logs from upstream: If a chip is unknown the user is asked to test and report the result to the mailing list. Having `-VE` listed as the last option can result in an unbootable system for users not knowing what the command does, since rebooting the system after that command is fatal since the flash chip is empty.  BUG=chromium:478356 BRANCH=none TEST=none  Change-Id: I43d9dd63f2c1cc58f2e98f19b290eb044e7c8890 Signed-off-by: Souvik Ghosh &lt;souvikghosh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/367102 Commit-Ready: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="367102" owner_email="souvikghosh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/02/367102/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id6e7d1b8409e02b59aa451448490badd09e25200" commit="89fd4ed81aa2da6b05b5d262305ae72b872ada09" commit_message="Warnings for one-time programmable (OTP) memory  Corresponds to r1493 from upstream. Commit log from upstream: Some flash chips contain OTP memory that we cannot read or write (yet). This prohibits us from cloning them, hence warn the user if we detect it. Not all variations of the tagged chips contain OTP memory. They are often only enabled on request or have there own ordering numbers. There is usually no way to distinguish them. Because this is a supposedly seldomly used feature the warning is shown in with dbg verbosity.  The manpage is extended to describe the backgrounds a bit.  This patch is based on the idea and code of Daniel Lenski.  BUG=chromium:478356 BRANCH=none TEST=needs testing  Change-Id: Id6e7d1b8409e02b59aa451448490badd09e25200 Signed-off-by: Souvik Ghosh &lt;souvikghosh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/368880 Commit-Ready: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="368880" owner_email="souvikghosh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/80/368880/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I228ea2e1e73081c05a99beea78af3c4195e8059b" commit="6c8989a161b93c6139157475e44d8a90861dc9f4" commit_message="ichspi.c - warn user and disable writes for a protected address range  Corresponds to r1494 from upstream. Commit log from upstream: This includes not only the notorious read-only flash descriptors and locked ME regions, but also the more rarely used PRs (Protected Ranges). The user can enforce write support by specifying ich_spi_force=yes in the programmer options, but we don't tell him the exact syntax interactively. He has to read it up in the man page.  BUG=chromium:478356 BRANCH=none TEST=none  Change-Id: I228ea2e1e73081c05a99beea78af3c4195e8059b Signed-off-by: Souvik Ghosh &lt;souvikghosh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/372463 Commit-Ready: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="372463" owner_email="souvikghosh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/63/372463/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1df5d0a15a6536e1ba267ef25767bd27edd61505" commit="c90ea0b362cc27feb1e61a0c94bacf8bb2f6a07c" commit_message="autoupdate_CatchBadSignatures: update test instructions  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55273,chromium:575960 TEST=Manually  Change-Id: I1df5d0a15a6536e1ba267ef25767bd27edd61505 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/375561 Commit-Ready: YH Lin &lt;yueherngl@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: YH Lin &lt;yueherngl@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Zeuthen &lt;zeuthen@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="375561" owner_email="yueherngl@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/61/375561/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Id8f98071f5f85c05c1d4257ac46fe01b5386f42e" commit="c46b4931c2656e9fbeb4381daa9a4791a8be784a" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Handle exiting process in audit_log_d_path.  If the process is existing, current-&gt;fs may be NULL, so we cannot resolve paths in audit messages.  BUG=chromium:639102 TEST=Ran on cyan.  Change-Id: Id8f98071f5f85c05c1d4257ac46fe01b5386f42e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/372981 Commit-Ready: Ricky Zhou &lt;rickyz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ricky Zhou &lt;rickyz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 4c2b0a35a4dc9269ed229628f2fc536c3c1ce14a) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/375538 Reviewed-by: Ricky Zhou &lt;rickyz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="375538" owner_email="rickyz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/38/375538/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iad52e6173a1f785e4d48ca5287a5c1dd2fce17ab" commit="3031dd5a7a9c05ac57af20f9cc136aa9ae4e3159" commit_message="Autotest: Add an Rpc Validator to limit RPCs that can only be called by master.  Some RPCs cannot be called by caller except master AFE, or it will lead to db inconsistency between shard and master.  This CL fixes this problem by adding an RPC validator to filter such calls from RPC handling side. The validor will refuse any calls whose caller is not master AFE but the target calling method is RPCs in shard.  BUG=chromium:635288 TEST=Testing with a cbf master and a cbf shard: shard works, jobs can be picked up, scheduled and worked. Check master/shard AFEs, can't see any missing contents.  Change-Id: Iad52e6173a1f785e4d48ca5287a5c1dd2fce17ab Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/374139 Commit-Ready: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="374139" owner_email="xixuan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/39/374139/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6f7daed9def77523935f357ffde6d486a3f4d680" commit="38fb9c21a4b1a737c44fe790a186e73ddcf7c540" commit_message="Revert &quot;chromeos_config: Disable veyron_rialto payload testing.&quot;  This reverts commit 5562b48f6b7bcd2f076228f3a055f9292f69fc5e.  BUG=chromium:621750 TEST=None  Change-Id: I6f7daed9def77523935f357ffde6d486a3f4d680 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/374098 Commit-Ready: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jonathan Dixon &lt;joth@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="374098" owner_email="dgarrett@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" p